WEBVTT

00:00.690 --> 00:03.370
Sort the expressions
according to their values.

00:03.370 --> 00:05.640
You can put any number
of cards in a category

00:05.640 --> 00:07.717
or leave a category empty.

00:07.717 --> 00:09.550
And so we have this
diagram right over here,

00:09.550 --> 00:12.310
then we have these cards
that have these expressions.

00:12.310 --> 00:15.416
And we're supposed to sort
these into different buckets.

00:15.416 --> 00:16.790
So we're trying
to say, well what

00:16.790 --> 00:20.000
is the length of segment AC
over the length of segment

00:20.000 --> 00:21.030
BC equal to?

00:21.030 --> 00:23.130
Which of these expressions
is it equal to?

00:23.130 --> 00:27.109
And then we should drag it
into the appropriate buckets.

00:27.109 --> 00:28.650
So to figure these
out, I've actually

00:28.650 --> 00:32.750
already redrawn this
problem on my little

00:32.750 --> 00:35.050
I guess you call it scratch
pad or blackboard, whatever

00:35.050 --> 00:36.220
you want to call it.

00:36.220 --> 00:37.960
This right over here
is that same diagram

00:37.960 --> 00:39.110
blown up a little bit.

00:39.110 --> 00:41.799
Here are the expressions that
we need to drag into things.

00:41.799 --> 00:43.340
And here are the
buckets that we need

00:43.340 --> 00:45.506
to see which of these
expressions are equal to which

00:45.506 --> 00:46.930
of these expressions.

00:46.930 --> 00:48.510
So let's first look at this.

00:48.510 --> 00:52.530
The length of segment AC over
the length of segment BC.

00:52.530 --> 00:54.089
So let's think about what AC is.

00:54.089 --> 00:55.130
The length of segment AC.

00:55.130 --> 00:57.460
AC is this right here.

00:57.460 --> 01:02.480
So it's this length right
over here in purple over

01:02.480 --> 01:07.280
the length of segment BC, over
this length right over here.

01:07.280 --> 01:11.040
So it's the ratio of
the lengths of two

01:11.040 --> 01:12.560
sides of a right triangle.

01:12.560 --> 01:17.525
This is clearly a right
triangle, triangle ABC.

01:17.525 --> 01:18.900
And I could color
that in just so

01:18.900 --> 01:20.608
you know what triangle
I'm talking about.

01:20.608 --> 01:24.730
Triangle ABC is
this entire triangle

01:24.730 --> 01:26.112
that we could focus on.

01:26.112 --> 01:27.820
So you could imagine
that it's reasonable

01:27.820 --> 01:29.820
that the ratio of two
sides of a right triangle

01:29.820 --> 01:32.440
are going to be the sine
of one of its angles.

01:32.440 --> 01:35.040
And they give us one of
the angles right over here.

01:35.040 --> 01:38.684
They give us this
angle right over here.

01:38.684 --> 01:40.600
You say, well all they
did is mark that angle.

01:40.600 --> 01:43.360
But notice, one arc is
here, one arc is here.

01:43.360 --> 01:46.880
So anywhere we see only one arc,
that's going to be 30 degrees.

01:46.880 --> 01:48.900
So this is 30 degrees as well.

01:48.900 --> 01:51.052
You have two arcs here,
that's 41 degrees.

01:51.052 --> 01:53.260
Two arcs here, this is going
to be congruent to that.

01:53.260 --> 01:55.070
This over here is
going to be 41 degrees.

01:55.070 --> 01:55.940
This is three arcs.

01:55.940 --> 01:58.360
They don't tell us how
many degrees that is,

01:58.360 --> 02:00.160
but this angle
with the three arcs

02:00.160 --> 02:02.380
is congruent to this
angle with the three arcs

02:02.380 --> 02:03.290
right over there.

02:03.290 --> 02:06.990
So anyway, this yellow
triangle, triangle ABC,

02:06.990 --> 02:10.620
we know the measure of
this angle is 30 degrees.

02:10.620 --> 02:12.590
And then they give
us these two sides.

02:12.590 --> 02:15.860
So how do these sides relate
to this 30 degree angle?

02:15.860 --> 02:18.610
Well, side AC is adjacent to it.

02:18.610 --> 02:22.270
It's literally, it's one of the
sides of the angle that is not

02:22.270 --> 02:25.190
the hypotenuse, so let
me write that down.

02:25.190 --> 02:26.606
This is adjacent.

02:29.140 --> 02:30.510
And what is BC?

02:30.510 --> 02:33.510
Well, BC is the hypotenuse
of this right triangle.

02:33.510 --> 02:36.030
It's the side opposite
the 90 degrees.

02:36.030 --> 02:38.860
So this is the hypotenuse.

02:38.860 --> 02:44.050
So what trig function,
when applied to 30 degrees,

02:44.050 --> 02:48.220
is equal to the adjacent
side over the hypotenuse?

02:48.220 --> 02:50.790
Let's write down sohcahtoa
just to remind ourselves.

02:50.790 --> 02:54.700
So soh cah toa.

02:54.700 --> 02:57.840
Sine of an angle is
opposite over hypotenuse,

02:57.840 --> 03:01.700
cosine of an angle is
adjacent over hypotenuse.

03:01.700 --> 03:06.950
So cosine, let's write this
down, cosine of 30 degrees

03:06.950 --> 03:11.580
is going to be equal to the
length of the adjacent side.

03:11.580 --> 03:17.080
So that is AC, over the length
of the hypotenuse, which

03:17.080 --> 03:18.840
is equal to BC.

03:18.840 --> 03:22.120
So this right over
here is the same thing

03:22.120 --> 03:25.300
as the cosine of 30 degrees.

03:25.300 --> 03:27.690
So let's drag it in there.

03:27.690 --> 03:33.070
This is equal to the
cosine of 30 degrees.

03:33.070 --> 03:35.700
Now let's look at the next one.

03:35.700 --> 03:36.976
Cosine of angle DEC.

03:39.500 --> 03:40.780
Where is DEC?

03:40.780 --> 03:46.680
So DEC-- D, E, C. So that's
this angle right over here.

03:46.680 --> 03:49.040
I'll put four arcs here so
we don't get it confused.

03:49.040 --> 03:50.790
So this is angle DEC.

03:50.790 --> 03:53.640
So what is the cosine of DEC?

03:53.640 --> 03:57.300
Well once again, cosine is
adjacent over hypotenuse.

03:57.300 --> 04:00.740
So cosine of angle DEC,
the adjacent side to this,

04:00.740 --> 04:02.986
well that's this
right over here.

04:02.986 --> 04:04.860
You might say, well
isn't this side adjacent?

04:04.860 --> 04:07.527
Well that side, side DE, that
is the actual hypotenuse.

04:07.527 --> 04:09.360
So that's not going to
be the adjacent side.

04:09.360 --> 04:14.060
So the adjacent side
is, I could call it EC.

04:14.060 --> 04:16.190
It's the length of segment EC.

04:16.190 --> 04:21.800
And then the hypotenuse
is this right over here.

04:21.800 --> 04:24.770
The length of the hypotenuse--
the hypotenuse is side DE,

04:24.770 --> 04:27.050
or ED, however you
want to call it.

04:27.050 --> 04:31.650
And so the length of it is,
we could just write it as DE.

04:31.650 --> 04:33.132
Now what is this also equal to?

04:33.132 --> 04:34.590
We don't see this
choice over here.

04:34.590 --> 04:37.970
We don't have the ratio EC
over DE as one of these choices

04:37.970 --> 04:39.170
here.

04:39.170 --> 04:42.050
But what we do have is one of--
we do get one of the angles

04:42.050 --> 04:42.550
here.

04:42.550 --> 04:44.880
They give us this 41 degrees.

04:44.880 --> 04:47.670
And the ratio of this green
side over-- the length

04:47.670 --> 04:50.380
of this green side over this
orange side, what would that

04:50.380 --> 04:52.010
be in terms of, if
we wanted to apply

04:52.010 --> 04:54.110
a trig function to this angle?

04:54.110 --> 04:56.840
Well, relative to this
angle, the green side

04:56.840 --> 04:59.240
is the opposite side,
and the orange side

04:59.240 --> 05:00.800
is still the hypotenuse.

05:00.800 --> 05:03.120
So relative to 41
degrees-- so let's

05:03.120 --> 05:06.190
write this down--
relative to 41 degrees,

05:06.190 --> 05:09.310
this ratio is the opposite
over the hypotenuse.

05:09.310 --> 05:11.470
It's the cosine of
this angle, but it's

05:11.470 --> 05:13.260
the sine of this
angle right over here.

05:13.260 --> 05:15.930
Sine is opposite
over hypotenuse.

05:15.930 --> 05:18.700
So this is equal to the sine
of this angle right over here.

05:18.700 --> 05:22.200
It's equal to the
sine of 41 degrees.

05:22.200 --> 05:24.790
So that is this one
right over here.

05:24.790 --> 05:29.430
The sine of 41 degrees.

05:29.430 --> 05:33.000
So let's drag that in to
the appropriate bucket.

05:35.850 --> 05:39.280
Sine of 41 degrees
is the same thing

05:39.280 --> 05:42.830
as the cosine of angle DEC.

05:42.830 --> 05:44.780
Only have two left.

05:44.780 --> 05:51.060
So now we have to figure out
what the sine of angle CDA is.

05:51.060 --> 05:53.890
So let's see, where is CDA?

05:53.890 --> 05:57.380
CDA is this entire angle.

05:57.380 --> 05:59.987
It's this entire
angle right over here.

05:59.987 --> 06:02.070
So I could put a bunch of
arcs here if I want just

06:02.070 --> 06:04.510
to show that it's different
than all the other ones.

06:04.510 --> 06:07.090
So that's that angle
right over there.

06:07.090 --> 06:11.950
So now we're really dealing
with this larger right triangle.

06:11.950 --> 06:13.850
Let me highlight it
in this pink color.

06:13.850 --> 06:18.340
So we're now dealing with
this larger right triangle

06:18.340 --> 06:19.289
right over here.

06:19.289 --> 06:21.080
We care about the sine
of this whole thing.

06:21.080 --> 06:23.003
Remember, sine is
opposite over hypotenuse.

06:26.250 --> 06:35.800
So the opposite side
is going to be side CA.

06:35.800 --> 06:40.700
So this is going to be
equal to the length of CA

06:40.700 --> 06:42.840
over the hypotenuse,
which is AD.

06:47.970 --> 06:52.080
So that is going to be over AD.

06:52.080 --> 06:55.520
And once again, we don't
see that as a choice here.

06:55.520 --> 06:59.260
But maybe we can express
this ratio-- maybe

06:59.260 --> 07:01.370
this ratio is a trig
function applied

07:01.370 --> 07:02.562
to one of the other angles.

07:02.562 --> 07:04.020
And they give us
one of the angles.

07:04.020 --> 07:05.686
They give us this
angle right over here.

07:05.686 --> 07:08.080
I guess we could
call this angle DAC.

07:08.080 --> 07:09.990
This is 30 degrees.

07:09.990 --> 07:12.145
So relative to this
angle, what two sides

07:12.145 --> 07:13.270
are we taking the ratio of?

07:13.270 --> 07:15.780
We're taking, now, the ratio
of, relative to this angle,

07:15.780 --> 07:19.850
the adjacent side
over the hypotenuse.

07:19.850 --> 07:22.440
So this is the adjacent
side over the hypotenuse.

07:22.440 --> 07:24.260
What deals with adjacent
over hypotenuse?

07:24.260 --> 07:25.840
Well, cosine.

07:25.840 --> 07:28.670
So this is equal to the
cosine of this angle.

07:28.670 --> 07:32.960
So this is equal to
cosine of 30 degrees.

07:32.960 --> 07:36.770
Sine of CDA is
equal to the cosine

07:36.770 --> 07:39.180
of this angle right over here.

07:39.180 --> 07:44.490
So this one is equal to
this right over here.

07:44.490 --> 07:48.730
So let me drag that in.

07:48.730 --> 07:52.182
So this one is equal to--
so you can see that I just

07:52.182 --> 07:53.510
dragged it in-- equal to that.

07:53.510 --> 07:55.320
Now we have one left.

07:55.320 --> 07:56.180
We have one left.

07:56.180 --> 07:58.740
Home stretch, we should
be getting excited.

07:58.740 --> 08:00.770
AE over EB.

08:00.770 --> 08:05.150
AE, let me use this color.

08:05.150 --> 08:06.450
Length of segment AE.

08:06.450 --> 08:08.820
That's this length
right over here.

08:08.820 --> 08:10.540
Let me make that stand out more.

08:10.540 --> 08:12.501
Let me do it in this red.

08:12.501 --> 08:16.240
This color right over here,
that's length of segment AE,

08:16.240 --> 08:18.734
over length of segment EB.

08:22.250 --> 08:25.180
This is EB right over here.

08:25.180 --> 08:27.320
This is EB.

08:27.320 --> 08:33.590
So now we are focused on this
right triangle right over here.

08:33.590 --> 08:35.890
Well, we know the measure
of this angle over here.

08:35.890 --> 08:42.270
We have double arcs
right over here,

08:42.270 --> 08:44.500
and they say this is 41 degrees.

08:44.500 --> 08:47.320
So we have double
marks over here,

08:47.320 --> 08:49.960
and this is also going
to be 41 degrees.

08:49.960 --> 08:52.620
So relative to this
angle, what ratio is this?

08:52.620 --> 08:56.860
This is the opposite
over the hypotenuse.

08:56.860 --> 08:59.900
Opposite over the hypotenuse,
this right over here

08:59.900 --> 09:04.090
is going to be sine of that
angle, sine of 41 degrees.

09:04.090 --> 09:07.460
So it's equal to this
first one right over there.

09:07.460 --> 09:10.950
So let's drag it.

09:10.950 --> 09:13.190
So this is going to be
equal to sine of 41 degrees.

09:13.190 --> 09:14.890
So none of the ones
actually ended up

09:14.890 --> 09:17.960
being equal to the
tangent of 41 degrees.

09:17.960 --> 09:20.440
Now let's see if we
actually got this right.

09:20.440 --> 09:22.100
I hope I did.

09:22.100 --> 09:23.830
We did.
